The problem is that out-of-range discounts are silently treated as “no discount” instead of being rejected:

```javascript
if (discountPercent < 0 || discountPercent > 100) {
    return price;
}
```

That is why `applyDiscount(50, 110)` returns `50`, and why `applyDiscount(50, -5)` also returns `50`. If invalid input should be an error, the function should throw instead of returning the original price.

